
AMISOR borehole AM03 MICROCAT data for 2011/2012 season
-------------------------------------------------------

Data from the sixth download.

ascii format
------------
contained in column formatted files catxxxx_6.dat, where
xxxx = microcat serial number. The columns are:

1. decimal time - decimal days, where 0.0 = 0000 on January 1st 2001.
So, for example, midday on 15th January 2001 is decimal time 14.5
2. temperature (deg. C, T90)
3. conductivity (mS/cm)
4. pressure (dbar)
5. salinity (PSS78)
6. to 11. day, month, year, hour, minute, second.

* Note that all times are UTC.

* There is a line of data for each recording interval (i.e. no gaps),
and null data is represented by -999.0

* There are no data for cat3883 - assumed flat battery.

* For cat4054, there are conductivity/salinity data spikes at the following times:
(note: not removed from the data)
1630 to 1800 on 10/01/2011
1600 to 1800 on 24/01/2011
1330 on 13/03/2011

* For cat4054, there is a temperature (and therefore salinity) data spikes at the following time:
(note: not removed from the data)
1930 on 25/05/2011

* For cat4055, there are conductivity/salinity data spikes at the following times:
(note: not removed from the data)
1100 to 1900 on 07/02/2011

* Linear clock correction applied to "compress" times, to correct
for clock drift. 

